# Force LF across platforms for files that MUST stay LF (Linux deployment).
# Without this, Windows Git may check these out as CRLF and break their shebang.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.conf     text eol=lf
Caddyfile  text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Everything else uses the platform default; binaries stay untouched.
*             text=auto
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.jpeg        binary
*.gif         binary
*.ico         binary
*.woff        binary
*.woff2       binary
*.ttf         binary
*.pdf         binary
*.sql         text

# NOTE: keep every source file UTF-8 WITHOUT a byte-order mark.
#
# A BOM before an opening <?php makes PHP emit three invisible bytes as
# output before any code runs. That blocks every header() call in the file
# ("headers already sent"), so session redirects are silently discarded and
# the page renders completely blank - no HTML, no sidebar, no error text.
# It is easy to add by accident (PowerShell 5.1 Set-Content -Encoding UTF8,
# some editors) and is invisible in most diffs.
#
# Git cannot strip a BOM that is already committed, so verify with:
#   powershell -File scripts/check-bom.ps1